// title: Ingestion Size Security Events · Unified XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Sentinel
// tables: SecurityEvent
// purpose: The query below returns the top 10 Windows Security Events with the biggest footprint in your Sentinel environment. The query can be used to determine value for money, as more events increase the cost of your Sentinel environment. The size of each event depends on the amount of data in the columns. 
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/SecurityEvents/IngestionSizeSecurityEvents.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
let SearchWindow = 90d;
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(SearchWindow)
| summarize TotalEvents = count(), Bytes=sum(_BilledSize), GBs= round(sum(_BilledSize) / (1024 * 1024 * 1024), 2) by EventID, Activity
| top 10 by Bytes
